	(text_box "Six TI TPS22918 load switches (contract §2: U901-U906). Chain: 5V0_SYS - SW1 (REQ_B) - SW_N1 - SW2a (PERMIT_OK) || SW2b (TEST_MODE_I) - SW_N2 - SW3 (HOLD_OK) - SW_N3 - SW4 (WIN_OPEN_I) - BRIDGE_5V. SW5 (SW5_ON = SEQ_HOLD AND NOT\nTEST_MODE) from 5V0_SYS straight to BRIDGE_5V (D-59: consent starts, hardware completes).\nEvery ON pin has a 100 k pull-down: an unpowered or open driver leaves its switch off. QOD is left open on all six: an enabled internal 25-ohm discharge on SW4 would load BRIDGE_5V while SW5 holds it, and on an inner node it would pull\ncurrent backwards through the other switches. Instead each inner node and the rail have their own bleed resistor.\nCT = 1 nF on every switch: whichever closes last sets a rise of about 2.5 ms (SLVSD76C Table 2), so the 220 uF hold-up on sheet 12 draws about 0.45 A, inside the 2 A rating.\nTPS22918 VOUT may exceed VIN (SW4 while SW5 holds the rail): outside the recommended conditions (VOUT <= VIN), inside the 6 V absolute maximum; any reverse current only feeds back towards 5V0_SYS and cannot create a consent (capture\nnotes, assumption A-3).\nBRIDGE_ARMED_N: 2N7002 pulls low once BRIDGE_5V passes about 1-2.5 V (VGS(th) 1-2.5 V, onsemi NDS7002A/D); pull-up is on sheet 04."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 269.05 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
