	)
	(text_box "Each clock: 100 k pull-down at the input (contract), then a two-pole RC low-pass (4.7 k / 3.9 nF, 47 k / 390 pF: each pole 8.7 kHz) and a 1 M pull-down at the Schmitt input, then an SN74LVC1G17 on the controller's own rail. The low-pass\nis placed BEFORE the Schmitt buffer, not between the buffer and the pump: a 100 kHz square wave reaches the Schmitt input as about 31-36 mV p-p (CALC, capture notes §3.1), far below its 0.51 V minimum hysteresis, so the buffer output\nstays static and the pump on sheet 11 gets no drive at all; 1-5 kHz squares (30-70 % duty) pass edge for edge. The buffer then drives the pump with its full 24 mA output, so the filter costs the pump nothing (WP-F's requirement: -7.0 V at\n1.1 mA from a 2 kHz 3.3 V clock).\nThe 1 M pull-down makes an open filter resistor read low (static), never floating.\nHOLD_A_DRV / HOLD_B_DRV pull-downs are on sheet 11 (contract §5.4)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 475.09 31.75 0)
		(size 268.565 14.954)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9dd873aa-0180-578c-a7f8-a541aee8eca0")
	)
	(text_box "Dynamic consent detector PERMIT_CLK -> PERMIT_OK on 3V3_SUP"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 763.975 25.4 0)
		(size 265.13 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
