		)
		(uuid "efcdebed-2035-5438-bd66-d04be514b7de")
	)
	(text_box "Band-limited pump detector (§B8.1, R-11). PERMIT_CLK: 100 k pull-down, two-pole low-pass (as the hold drives), 1 M pull-down, SN74LVC2G14 on 3V3_SUP: gate 1 squares and inverts, gate 2 re-inverts, so every clock edge (rising or\nfalling) is a rising edge on one of the two pump phases.\nEach phase: 470 ohm, TWO 220 nF C0G in series (one shorted capacitor still blocks DC), BAV99 series pair (pin 1 anode to GND, pin 3 common = pump node, pin 2 cathode to the hold node). Hold node PD_H: 100 nF C0G with 2 x 71.5 k in\nparallel (35.75 k; one open resistor only doubles the time constant). Comparator TLV7031 (push-pull; held LOW by its power-on reset below 1.6 V supply, SLVSE13J §6.3): IN+ = hold node, IN- = 0.30 x 3V3_SUP from 2 x 464 k in parallel\nover 100 k (one open top resistor lowers the threshold to 0.18 x 3V3_SUP, never to zero).\nBehaviour [CALC, behavioural model, capture notes §3.2]: valid <= 0.1 ms after the first edges at 1 kHz; stays valid >= 3.35 ms after the last edge (firmware gap <= 1 ms: margin 3.3x); invalid <= 7.4 ms after the last edge from 5 kHz;\nDC gives nothing; >= 100 kHz never reaches the pump (static Schmitt). Supply is the supervisor's rail: supervisor off = no output (pull-down on PERMIT_OK).\nOne single transition of PERMIT_CLK (one edge) DOES give a valid output for about 3-7 ms; documented in the capture notes (bounded by the 20 ms rail-ready delay on sheet 12 and the window)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 763.975 31.75 0)
		(size 265.13 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "86334b53-9fe1-5c1c-9712-a9fa392ea87b")
	)
