	(text_box "HOLD_A_HELD_N / HOLD_B_HELD_N: 10 k pull-ups to 5V0_SYS (contract §5.4) plus a 1 M backup each, because the opto is open-collector and 'dark' is a normal state: with only one resistor, that resistor opening would leave a CMOS\ninput floating, which could read 'held'. Low only when the stack's opto LED is lit by the real negative hold bias. HOLD_OK = NOR (SN74LVC1G02 on 5V0_SYS): high only when both are actively pulled low. Open opto, open wire,\nunpowered sheet 11: the pull-up reads 'not held'. Unpowered or open NOR output: the 100 k pull-down on HOLD_OK (SW3 ON) reads 'not held'.\nOne HOLD_OK feeds SW3, the charger gates and the window-start AND: a stuck-high NOR is therefore seen by the daily blocking tests F-8 (c)/(d), which release one hold and expect BRIDGE_ARMED_N high.\nHOLD_RB_A_N / HOLD_RB_B_N: SN74LVC2G07 open-drain copies (low = held), pull-ups on sheet 04; 5V0_SYS off = released = 'not held'."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 600.22 225.012 0)
		(size 256.51 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
