	)
	(text_box "CHAIN = REQ_B AND HOLD_OK AND (PERMIT_OK OR TEST_MODE) - the logical 'SW1-SW3 all on' (capture notes DEP-3: logic, not the SW_N3 voltage, so a rail held by SW5 cannot fake or mask the start). Its rising edge clocks WSTART\n(SN74LVC2G74, D = 1): the start is latched, so a toggling consent cannot restart the window. WSTART charges 1.47 M / 100 nF C0G; TLV7031 compares with 0.640 x 5V0_SYS (56.2 k / 100 k): WIN_OPEN_I high while below = 138-163 ms [CALC].\nRatiometric: supply variation cancels.\nRe-arm: ANY_N = NOR(REQ_B, PERMIT_OK OR TEST_OK) high only with every consent absent. It charges 549 k / 100 nF; TLV7041 (open drain) pulls REARM_N low after 51-60 ms [CALC] and clears WSTART; any consent returning discharges the RC\nat once through the BAS116. Open-drain + 100 k pull-up: a dead re-arm comparator never re-arms (window stays closed after use).\nBAS116 diodes empty each RC quickly when its driver goes low (low leakage, 5 nA at 75 V: negligible against 1.47 M).\nPower-up: WSTART is undefined (SCES203Q states no power-up state); either state is safe: open until the first chain edge, or open 150 ms then closed until re-arm (capture notes §5).\nWIN_OPEN_I drives SW4 and, through 1 k, the global WIN_OPEN to sheet 12 (100 k pull-down and Ioff buffer there)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.18 370.776 0)
		(size 263.8 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
